        {
          "id": 5197,
          "text": "Notion integration FAQs",
          "highlight": false,
          "color": "#475467",
          "bold": false
        }
      ],
      "faqList": [
        {
          "id": 2774,
          "header": "What does the Notion integration do?",
          "body": "It syncs form submissions to a Notion database automatically — each response becomes an entry with your form fields as properties.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        },
        {
          "id": 2773,
          "header": "How do I connect Notion?",
          "body": "From your form's Automate tab, add the Notion integration, authorize your workspace, pick the destination database, and publish.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        },
        {
          "id": 2775,
          "header": "Can different forms feed different databases?",
          "body": "Yes — the integration is configured per form, so each form can sync to its own database.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        },
        {
          "id": 2776,
          "header": "What if syncing stops?",
          "body": "Reconnect Notion from the Automate tab. Your submissions always remain safely stored in Formester.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        },
        {
          "id": 2777,
          "header": "What is Formester?",
          "body": "Formester is an online form builder for creating forms, surveys, and quizzes with a drag-and-drop editor or AI. It connects with the tools your team already uses — Google Sheets, Slack, HubSpot, Zapier, and more — so your form data flows wherever you need it.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        }
      ]
    },
